window.docContents[200].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Pqxdh.Security.Headline/#file-Computational___Specifications___Pqxdh___Security___Headline":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Pqxdh/Security › Headline.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the computational proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 177 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\n\n\nReduction bundles for the one-key PQXDH headline statementTrusted: the statement. This file defines the one-key KeyInd reduction bundles and boundedness predicates used by PqxdhCorrectAndSecureδ (HeadlineDelta.lean) and the CLI security statements (Computational/Specifications/LibsignalCli/StatementPqElf.lean). Companion one-key first-message Auth reduction bundles are in Auth/Headline.lean. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.For each query budget b and b-bounded game adversary A, a reduction family packages the adversaries against GapSigEufCma, KemShCr, and GapDhWithSign constructed from A for the one-key random-oracle PQXDH handshake game (KeyInd1KeyRo.lean). Each reduction is represented as a first-order ReductionDsl syntax tree (CostedReduction or TwoStageCostedReduction) over the pure operation table pqAtomicOps and coin-only sampler table pqAtomicSamplers, so step cost, output block sizes, and worst-case query counts are checked syntactically.The two-stage KemShCr reduction runs both stages with fuel := b.q_total; because a b-bounded adversary makes at most b.q_total game queries in total, fuel is never exhausted and the fallback return value is unreachable. Syntactic bounds (KeyIndCostedReductionBounds) check both the uniform stepCostBudget S b over b.q_total handled queries and the online/random-oracle split budget stepCostBudgetSplit S b b.q_ro via CostBoundedByKind, while semantic compliance (KeyIndReductionQueryBounds) enforces the sharper dynamic caps q_sig = 2 * min S.N_spk_tot S.N_recv and q_ddh = gdhQueryBudget S b declared by KeyIndCostedReductionFamily.eval.\n\n\n\nReduction bundles\n\nstructure KeyIndReductionFamilyL51–56 ↗#Shallow reduction family mapping each b-bounded KeyIndAdversary S to adversaries against GapSigEufCma (sig), KemShCr (shcr), and GapDhWithSign (gdh).\n\nstructure KeyIndCostedReductionFamilyL58–67 ↗#Deep-embedded ReductionDsl syntax trees over pqAtomicOps and pqKeyIndCodec S for the GapSigEufCma (sig), KemShCr (shcr), and GapDhWithSign (gdh) reductions.\n\ndef KeyIndCostedReductionFamily.evalL69–89 ↗#Interpret a KeyIndCostedReductionFamily into a KeyIndReductionFamily at fuel := b.q_total with fallback false for shcr.\n\nCost, block-size, and query bounds\n\ndef keyIndQueryKindL93–97 ↗#Classifies KeyIndQuery into online queries (0, matching isKeyIndOnlineQuery) and offline .roQuery random-oracle queries (1) for per-kind step-cost accounting.\n\ndef keyIndKindCountsL99–103 ↗#Per-kind query caps for a b-bounded KeyIndAdversary: min b.q_on b.q_total online queries (0) and min b.q_ro b.q_total random-oracle queries (1).\n\nstructure KeyIndCostedReductionBoundsL105–141 ↗#Syntactic resource bounds for R: size-honesty of pqAtomicOps and pqAtomicSamplers, uniform (stepCostBudget) and online/random-oracle split (stepCostBudgetSplit) step-cost bounds, worst-case query bounds over b.q_total handled queries, and run-local output block-size bounds.\n\nstructure KeyIndReductionQueryBoundsL143–148 ↗#Semantic query compliance of R: for every budget b and b-bounded adversary A, the evaluated sig, shcr, and gdh adversaries satisfy their .Bounded query predicates.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Pqxdh/Security/Headline.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Pqxdh.Security.Headline/#file-Computational___Specifications___Pqxdh___Security___Headline"},"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.SignalSession.CliRun/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___SignalSession___CliRun":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications/SignalSession › CliRun.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the symbolic proof 6 headline theorems depend on it 7 of 151 lines trusted trust banner B2, trusted: definitions used by the statement source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\n\n\nThe free choices\n\nstructure CliHooksL143–149 ↗#Abstract primitive bundle (the W parameter of the symbolic CLI statements in ElfBinding.lean / Binary.lean, guarded per input against realCliHooks).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/SignalSession/CliRun.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/LibsignalBinary___Specifications___/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.SignalSession.CliRun/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___SignalSession___CliRun"}});